 miss them people tend  to remember and then when you set the  same deadline again a year later they  certainly remember it are we going to be  saying let's have the fight to say  christmas in three weeks to flatten the  curve in 2024 2025 because it seems to  me that anna's logic means we would  anna do you think that we should be  wearing master in in restaurants  well i think that there's a good  argument for it but i would be always  guided by the science look i think the  real problem about masks is  notwithstanding that we have a prime  minister who has a problem in wearing a  mask and too many conservative mps who  seem to have a problem with wearing  masks but also if you go into a lot of  shops if you go into other public places  you're getting mixed messages from a lot  of the staff because they're not what  they're wearing masks either so one of  the things i would say is we need  clarity i mean i don't always wear a  mask so i forget to take it with me if  you go into a shop you go into a place  and the person people working there  aren't wearing them you kind of think oh  well there's no point so i we need  clarity that's the thing about good  public health messaging it needs to be  good and clear but you know this i mean  i'm not getting i don't get this thing  about you know we've got a saved  christmas and all the rest of it what we  have got to do is make sure and it's not  empty rhetoric we need to make sure that  we stop the spread of the virus in a way  that damages our nhs and it causes more  people to die and at the moment we have  this new variant we don't know a lot  about it so let's be guided by the  scientists who certainly know more i put  my hands up than i know and i don't have  a problem in following their guidance  but this idea that we're going to be  locked up in our homes until 2025 and  all the rest of it  i think that's that's a gross  exaggeration as i say what we need is  good clear  leadership we need good clear public  health